        <mxCell id="Za8gHh4nOocKNEtNeua0-17" value="&lt;br&gt;&lt;code&gt;git add&lt;/code&gt; command, you&#39;re &lt;strong&gt;staging&lt;/strong&gt; your changes. It means you&#39;re marking files or changes to be included in the next commit&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;The command to stage the file which is need to be commited in the local as well if needed in cloud git&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;for eg:&lt;br&gt;file change is needed means stage it&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;if not leave it simple this will not reflect in the repo&#39;s&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
